OL,3,GNEWSAMerseyrail boss defends e-bikes
OL,4,Aban
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe managing director of Merseyrail has
OL,7,Fdefended a ban on non-folding e-bikes
OL,8,Fon its trains and stations, insisting
OL,9,Fthe measures are needed to improve
OL,10,Fsafety and the risk is "really
OL,11,Fserious".
OL,13,FThe new rules were introduced during
OL,14,Fthe summer with Merseyrail citing
OL,15,Fsafety fears over battery fires, but
OL,16,Fthe ban will be enforced from January
OL,17,Fmeaning passengers who bring e-bikes
OL,18,Fcould face a fine.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,405,400,260,160,0,100
